<title>UK: UK '96 oil/gas receipts up 19 pct to 21 bln stg-Bank.</title>
<headline>UK '96 oil/gas receipts up 19 pct to 21 bln stg-Bank.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>British oil and gas revenues last year rose 19 percent to 20.93 billion stg, the Royal Bank of Scotland said on Friday.</p>
<p>Oil revenues, buoyed by crude prices at six-year highs, rose to 12.26 billion stg, the Bank said.</p>
<p>Gas revenues increased to 8.67 billion.</p>
<p>Oil production for the year was little changed at 2.54 million barrels a day (bpd).</p>
<p>Daily December oil revenues rose three percent on the month to 38.6 million stg.</p>
<p>Daily December gas revenues increased by 13.4 percent to 20.8 million stg a day.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
